# A fourth native expert weight format: IQ2_S (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B), through the
# pattern, validation, CPU tier and per-expert OpenCL kernels.
#
# Design:   docs/design-qwen35moe-serving-shape.md (patch 0050, 2026-09-24)
# Campaign: docs/campaigns/sub4bit-vram-kernel.md
#
# Prerequisite patches: 0039/0040 (per-expert kernel + dispatch), 0043 (native
# formats through the tier), 0045 (native per-expert OpenCL decode), 0047
# (resident slot pool), 0049 (pinned NVMe transport).
#
# `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` (`general.architecture = qwen35moe`) carries its experts as
# IQ2_S (ggml type 22) gate/up on all 40 layers over IQ3_XXS (37 layers) /
# IQ4_XS (3 layers) down. IQ2_S is not one of patch 0043's three formats:
#   - the weight is one 10-bit grid index per EIGHT values (four per 32),
#     packed as little-endian u16 in a u8 slot [E, out, K/32, 8];
#   - the sign byte is RAW (bit j flips value j; no 7-bit table index);
#   - there are TWO 4-bit sub-block scales per 32 values (the low nibble's for
#     values 0..15, the high nibble's for 16..31), stored as f16
#     [E, out, K/32, 2].
# IQ4_XS needs no new format: its split folds the 6-bit sub-block scales into
# the per-32 f32 scale and lands on the IQ4_NL layout patch 0043 already
# carries (tools/q4e/native_blocks.py iq4_xs_split -> iq4_nl_decode; measured
# 2026-09-24 on blk.34/38/39.ffn_down_exps, max|diff| 0.0 vs gguf-py), so the
# three IQ4_XS down tensors ride kWeightFormatIq4Nl unchanged.
#
# What this patch adds:
#   * MOECompressed::kWeightFormatIq2S = 4 + is_native_format, and the
#     [E, ofm, K/32, 8] weight-shape branch in validate_and_infer_types.
#   * NativeIq2sWeightsBlock (pattern_blocks/native_expert_block.{hpp,cpp}) and
#     its resolution in ConvertTiledMoeBlockNativeToMoeCompressed: the weight
#     u8 Constant is the 10-bit grid indices, the zero-point u8 Constant the
#     raw sign bytes, the f16 [.,2] scale the two sub-block scales.
#   * the CPU tier row decoder (moe_cpu_expert.cpp decode_native_row, format 4)
#     and kIq2sGrid[8192] transcribed from llama.cpp ggml-common.h.
#   * the OpenCL decode (native_dot_iq2s in moe_expert_swiglu.cl) and its
#     dispatch for the gate/up native kernels; the down kernel keeps IQ4_NL /
#     IQ3_XXS / Q8_0 (this checkpoint has no IQ2_S down).
#   * moe_otd_runtime.cpp skips the device scale transpose for IQ2_S (its two
#     sub-scales are read row-major) and a red-first unit cell for the decoder.
#
# Built clean on the pinned OpenVINO tree 2026-09-24: `ninja -j6
# openvino_intel_gpu_plugin` in the production build dir, rc 0 (47
# targets, the plugin links). The plugin unit cell
# `moe_cpu_expert_native.iq2_s_row_decodes_...` compiles to an object with the
# plugin's own flags and the vendored gtest headers (that build dir has no unit
# test target configured). The emitter side is tools/q4e/serving_shape.py's
# IQ2_S branch and build_qwen35moe_serving_shape_ir; byte-exactness of the
# emitted blocks against the GGUF is pinned by tests/python. A walker PASS is
# not a compile and no card compile is claimed: the A770 window is the next leg.

