+    // patch 0050. ic=64, two 32-value groups. Group 0: all four grid indices 0
+    // (grid[0] = eight 8s), sign byte 0x03 flips values 0 and 1, s0 = 1.0 for
+    // values 0..15, s1 = 2.0 for 16..31. Group 1: l=0 index 256 (LE bytes
+    // 00 01; grid[256] = 25,25,25,25,25,8,25,8), l=1..3 index 1023 (LE bytes
+    // FF 03; grid[1023] = eight 43s), no signs, s0 = s1 = 1.0. The 10-bit
+    // index is the point: the low byte alone gives 0, the assembly gives 256.
